<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">San Miguel de Tucumán</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">San Miguel de Tucumán is a city in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argentina">Argentina</a>, capital of Tucumán Province. Founded in 1565 by Diego de Villarroel and moved to its present site in 1685, it hosted the Congress of Tucumán, which declared the independence of the United Provinces of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-america">South America</a> on 9 July 1816. It is the centre of Argentina's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sugar-plantation">sugar</a> industry.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/san-miguel-de-tucuman.jpg" alt="San Miguel de Tucumán" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: gonzaloluciani · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tucuman_San_Miguel_ciudad_capital_vista_de_noche_contexto_srl_revista_gonzaloluciani.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
